course: dictionary
lesson: 15778
title: Twins
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A twin is one of two children born to the same mother at the same birth. Twins are a noun, so you can have a twin, or two twins. «Mia and Sam are twins, and they share the same birthday.» Here twins means the two children together.
explain: Some twins look almost the same. These are identical twins, and they come from one egg that splits in two. Other twins, called non-identical or fraternal twins, come from two eggs. They can be a boy and a girl and look quite different. «Identical twins» and «non-identical twins» are both kinds of twins.
explain: Twin can also be an adjective, meaning one of a matching pair. «Our room has twin beds, one on each side of the window.» A twin town is different: it is a town in another country that is friends with yours and visits it. «Our town is twinned with a town in France.»
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. If it talks about a mother, a birth, or two brothers or sisters, the word means people. If it talks about two matching things, like beds or towers, the word is an adjective.
fact: Twins are two children born to the same mother at the same birth.
fact: Identical twins come from one egg that splits, so they look almost the same.
fact: Non-identical (fraternal) twins come from two eggs and may be a boy and a girl.
fact: Twin (adjective) means one of a matching pair, as in «twin towers».
fact: «Twin towns» are towns in different countries that are friends and visit each other.
fact: Identical twins have the same genes, but they still have different fingerprints and personalities.
fact: In maths, «twin primes» are two primes that differ by 2, like 11 and 13.
exercise: «Mia and Sam are twins, born to the same mother on the same day.» What are twins? | Two friends who live on the same street | *Two children born to the same mother at the same birth | Two dogs born in the same litter | Two cousins who share a birthday
exercise: «Our room has twin beds, one on each side of the window.» What does twin mean in twin beds? | Painted blue | Very old | *One of a matching pair | Tiny
exercise: «Identical twins come from one egg that splits in two.» Why do identical twins look almost the same? | They are always the same height | *They come from one egg that splits | They have the same favourite food | They come from two eggs
test: «Our town is twinned with a town in Spain, and we visit each other every summer.» What is a twin town? | A town where all the houses match | A town with two names | A town with two big rivers | *A town in another country that is friends with yours
test: «Lena and her twin brother Max both love football.» Which kind of word is twin in this sentence? | A question word | A number | A verb | *A noun, part of the phrase twin brother
exam: «Non-identical twins come from two eggs, so they may be a boy and a girl.» What does the sentence tell you about non-identical twins? | They are always two girls | *They can look quite different from each other | They always look exactly the same | They come from one egg
